{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"# Hand-built LLM sub-calls bypass the model-class config and go to direct Anthropic\n\n## Scope: FOUR sites, one root cause, one fix shape\n\nEach builds a `RunRequest` by hand with `config=cfg` and declares no model class, so it inherits\n`cfg.model` regardless of how the three model classes are configured. MEASURED, not inferred — see\nthe comments for the full experiment:\n\n    llm/overlap/judge.py:46              op=overlap-judge    18 calls   <-- 18 of 23 in a plan review\n    llm/enrich.py:81                     op=ticket-digest     1 call    <-- runs on the STORE WRITE path\n    llm/operations.py:177                op=ticket-quality    1 call\n    llm/code_review/workflow_ops.py:571  op=code-novelty      1 call    <-- the site originally filed\n\nEverything else honours the configuration: all four plan-review passes, the completion verifier, and\nall seven code-review workflow steps.\n\n## Why this matters beyond consistency\n\nBedrock is normally chosen for data-residency, procurement or contractual reasons. These calls send\nreal content to direct Anthropic: the diff and prior findings (`code-novelty`), ticket text\n(`ticket-digest`, `ticket-quality`), and ticket digests for pairwise comparison (`overlap-judge`).\n\n**`overlap-judge` dominates plan-review traffic** — 18 of 23 calls. An operator who cuts over by\nconfiguring the three classes (the documented mechanism, and the one story eb6e will use) leaves the\nMAJORITY of plan-review traffic on direct Anthropic.\n\n**`ticket-digest` is the most insidious** because it is not in a gate at all: `enrich_drain.maybe_drain`\nis called from `_store/event_append.py:609` and `_store/push.py:295`, so it runs on the ticket STORE\nWRITE path — on ordinary `rebar comment` / `rebar create` calls, with no gate invocation and nothing\nin any verdict to reveal it.\n\n## The two configurations, and why both are needed\n\n* classes on Bedrock, `cfg.model` left bare-anthropic → the four sites above show `anthropic`: they\n  bypass the class config. This is the defect.\n* classes AND `cfg.model` on Bedrock → 15 calls, 0 on anthropic: nothing is HARDCODED past config.\n\nThe second configuration passes even with this bug unfixed, because a bypassing call inherits\n`cfg.model`. Any regression test must therefore pin the FIRST configuration, or it proves nothing.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] with the three model classes configured on a non-default provider and `cfg.model` left on the\n      default provider, NO call in review-plan, review, review-code or verify-completion resolves to\n      the `cfg.model` provider — asserted from a run's usage log, which `step`/`model_class` (story\n      b690) now makes readable per call\n- [ ] each of the four sites selects its model from the class vocabulary, and the class chosen for\n      each is stated in the code with its reason rather than left implicit\n- [ ] `code-novelty`'s choice is consistent with plan-review's novelty sub-call, or the difference is\n      documented as deliberate at both sites — `score_code_novelty`'s docstring currently claims it\n      \"mirrors\" `_score_floor_novelty`, which uses `_verifier_cfg`, and that parity does not hold\n- [ ] a test fails if ANY hand-built sub-call inherits `cfg.model` while a class table is configured\n      — the general defect, so a future hand-built sub-call cannot silently reintroduce it. A test\n      that enumerates today's four sites by name does NOT satisfy this\n- [ ] the `overlap-judge` test constructs its trigger deliberately: `wire.py:overlap_findings` runs\n      the judge only when BM25F retrieval returns candidates (`if not candidates: return []`, with\n      the query's own graph excluded), so a test that merely runs a gate and hopes the judge fires\n      will silently pass while testing nothing — both probes during the investigation hit exactly\n      that and produced zero judge calls\n- [ ] `ticket-digest`'s fix holds on the STORE WRITE path, not only inside a gate run\n- [ ] fail-safe behaviour is preserved at every site: the novelty signal must still degrade to\n      \"keep more findings\", and the overlap step must remain advisory and never block a review\n\n## Not in scope\n\nSibling `03b0` (a configured Bedrock provider is dropped for colon-bearing model ids) is a different\nseam — that one breaks the configuration before it is read; this one ignores it after."}},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1785624145925543001,"uuid":"afb003cf-9df8-4d37-b41c-b1a84c291cc2"}